! versions-late-version-object
!
! The Version object of this file sits deliberately far down, behind a comment header
! wider than ten kilobytes. Nothing below this header is unusual: the header itself is
! the reproducer, and the filler lines that follow exist only to push the Version object
! past a byte offset that one implementation treats as the end of the searchable region.
!
! Three files in the EnergyPlus 26.1.0 example set are shaped exactly like this:
!   RefBldgPrimarySchoolNew2004_Chicago.idf         Version at byte 10509
!   EMSCurveOverride_PackagedTerminalHeatPump.idf   Version at byte 12990
!   1ZoneWith14ControlledHeat-CoolPanels.idf        Version at byte 16547
!
! The first of those carries a 10507 byte comment header of exactly this kind, so the
! shape below is not contrived. It is the DOE reference building header, reduced.
!
! Filler. This line exists to widen the comment header. EnergyPlus reads the whole
! file before it looks for the Version object, so a header of any width is legal.
! Filler. This line exists to widen the comment header. EnergyPlus reads the whole
! file before it looks for the Version object, so a header of any width is legal.
